1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,920
CHANDLER! CHANDLER!

2
00:00:02,962 --> 00:00:04,045
( grunting )

3
00:00:04,087 --> 00:00:06,340
CHANDLER, I SAW WHAT
YOU WERE DOING

4
00:00:06,381 --> 00:00:07,758
THROUGH THE WINDOW!

5
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,552
I SAW WHAT YOU WERE DOING
TO MY SISTER!

6
00:00:10,594 --> 00:00:12,220
NOW, GET OUT HERE!

7
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:14,556
WELL, LISTEN,
WE HAD A GOOD RUN.

8
00:00:14,598 --> 00:00:16,851
YOU KNOW, WHAT WAS IT--
FOUR, FIVE MONTHS?

9
00:00:16,892 --> 00:00:19,144
I MEAN, THAT'S MORE
THAN MOST PEOPLE HAVE

10
00:00:19,186 --> 00:00:20,354
IN A LIFETIME.

11
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:22,690
SO, GOOD-BYE, TAKE CARE,
BYE-BYE, DEAR.

12
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:24,441
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

13
00:00:24,483 --> 00:00:26,151
OH, I'M GOING
ON THE LAM.

14
00:00:26,193 --> 00:00:28,069
COME ON, CHANDLER,
COME ON.

15
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:29,655
I CAN HANDLE ROSS.

16
00:00:29,697 --> 00:00:31,156
HOLD ON.

17
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:36,578
HEY, ROSS.
WHAT'S UP, BRO?

18
00:00:38,706 --> 00:00:39,999
WHAT...

19
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,375
THE HELL...

20
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:42,751
ARE YOU DOING?!

21
00:00:42,793 --> 00:00:44,043
HEY, WHAT'S GOING ON?

22
00:00:44,085 --> 00:00:45,587
WELL, I THINK...

23
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:48,256
I THINK ROSS KNOWS
ABOUT ME AND MONICA?

24
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:51,176
DUDE, HE'S RIGHT THERE...

25
00:00:53,971 --> 00:00:55,806
I THOUGHT YOU WERE
MY BEST FRIEND.

26
00:00:55,848 --> 00:00:57,056
THIS IS MY SISTER!

27
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:59,267
MY BEST FRIEND AND MY SISTER.

28
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:00,561
I CANNOT BELIEVE THIS!

29
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:03,188
LOOK, WE'RE NOT JUST
MESSING AROUND.

30
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:04,690
I LOVE HER, OKAY?

31
00:01:04,732 --> 00:01:06,525
I'M IN LOVE WITH HER.

32
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:10,696
I'M SO SORRY THAT YOU
HAD TO FIND OUT THIS WAY.

33
00:01:10,738 --> 00:01:13,407
I'M SORRY, BUT IT-IT'S TRUE.

34
00:01:13,448 --> 00:01:15,075
I-I LOVE HIM, TOO.

35
00:01:20,956 --> 00:01:23,792
MY BEST FRIEND
AND MY SISTER!

36
00:01:23,834 --> 00:01:26,461
I'M SO HAPPY!

37
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:29,088
I CANNOT BELIEVE THIS!

38
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:31,050
OH, I'M SORRY,
YOU GUYS WANT

39
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:33,635
TO PROBABLY GET SOME
HUGS IN, TOO, HUH?

40
00:01:33,677 --> 00:01:34,845
BIG NEWS!

41
00:01:34,887 --> 00:01:36,179
OH, NO, THAT'S OKAY.

42
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:38,348
WE'VE ACTUALLY KNOWN
FOR A WHILE.

43
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:42,770
WHAT-WHAT?

44
00:01:42,811 --> 00:01:44,271
YOU GUYS KNEW?

45
00:01:44,312 --> 00:01:45,647
YOU ALL KNEW

46
00:01:45,689 --> 00:01:47,858
AND YOU DIDN'T TELL ME?!

47
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:50,485
WELL, ROSS, WE WERE
WORRIED ABOUT YOU, OKAY?

48
00:01:50,527 --> 00:01:53,113
WE DIDN'T KNOW HOW
YOU WERE GOING TO REACT.

49
00:01:53,154 --> 00:01:54,573
MMM.

50
00:01:54,615 --> 00:01:58,368
YOU WERE WORRIED ABOUT ME?

51
00:01:58,410 --> 00:02:01,789
YOU DIDN'T KNOW HOW
I WAS GOING TO REACT?

52
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:05,626
OKAY, ALL RIGHT.

53
00:02:05,667 --> 00:02:07,002
WHEW!

54
00:02:07,044 --> 00:02:08,963
WHAT DO YOU SAY WE ALL,
UH, CLEAR OUT OF HERE

55
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:11,548
AND LET THESE TWO LOVEBIRDS
GET BACK DOWN TO BUSINESS?

56
00:02:14,175 --> 00:02:16,553
HEY, HEY, HEY,
I-I'M JUST TALKING HERE.

57
00:02:16,595 --> 00:02:18,513
HE'S THE ONE
DOING YOUR SISTER.

58
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:31,652
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

59
00:02:31,693 --> 00:02:33,904
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

60
00:02:33,946 --> 00:02:36,615
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

61
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:41,411
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

62
00:02:41,453 --> 00:02:43,914
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

63
00:02:43,956 --> 00:02:46,374
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

64
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:50,462
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

65
00:02:50,504 --> 00:02:56,384
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

66
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:03,182
HEY, YOU KNOW
WHAT I JUST REALIZED?

67
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:04,893
IF YOU GUYS EVER HAVE KIDS...

68
00:03:04,935 --> 00:03:06,269
WHOA, WHOA,
WE'RE HAVING KIDS?

69
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:07,813
I CALL GODFATHER.

70
00:03:09,481 --> 00:03:11,525
YOU CAN'T JUST CALL
GODFATHER.

71
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:15,821
DON'T YOU THINK HER BROTHER
SHOULD BE GODFATHER?

72
00:03:15,863 --> 00:03:18,448
SURE, IF YOU CARED ENOUGH
TO CALL IT FIRST.

73
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:19,658
YOU GUYS...

74
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:22,036
I THINK YOU'RE A FEW
STEPS AHEAD OF US.

75
00:03:22,077 --> 00:03:24,621
YEAH. BIG ZERO-GRAVITY
MOON STEPS.

76
00:03:24,663 --> 00:03:26,040
OH, I JUST THOUGHT

77
00:03:26,081 --> 00:03:27,708
OF THE GREATEST WEDDING GIFT
TO GET YOU.

78
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,250
OOH, I'LL GO IN
ON THAT WITH YOU.

79
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:30,669
I COULDN'T THINK
OF ANYTHING.

80
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:34,422
OH. HI, KATIE.

81
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:36,050
HEY, EVERYONE,
THIS IS KATIE.
HI.

82
00:03:36,091 --> 00:03:37,592
Joey:
SO, ARE YOU
READY TO GO?

83
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:39,636
I JUST GOT TO RUN
TO THE BATHROOM.
BACK THERE.

84
00:03:39,678 --> 00:03:40,929
HEY, WHERE WE GOING
TO LUNCH?

85
00:03:40,971 --> 00:03:42,931
I WAS THINKING
MAYBE CHINESE FOOD.

86
00:03:42,973 --> 00:03:45,266
OH, I LOVE CHINESE!

87
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,435
HOW'D YOU KNOW
I LOVE CHINESE?!

88
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:51,606
SHE IS SO CUTE.

89
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:54,860
YOU COULD FIT HER
RIGHT IN YOUR LITTLE POCKET.

90
00:03:54,902 --> 00:03:56,862
I DON'T KNOW...

91
00:03:56,904 --> 00:04:00,407
I MEAN, I LIKE HER A LOT,
AND SHE'S REALLY NICE, BUT...

92
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:01,324
BUT WHAT?

93
00:04:03,118 --> 00:04:06,163
SHE KEEPS PUNCHING ME.

94
00:04:06,205 --> 00:04:07,497
( chuckling )

95
00:04:07,539 --> 00:04:10,709
IN THAT CUTE, LITTLE
SWEET WAY SHE JUST DID?

96
00:04:10,751 --> 00:04:14,629
HEY, IT'S A LOT HARDER
THAN IT LOOKS, OKAY?

97
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:17,216
SHE-SHE... SHE'S HURTING ME.

98
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:19,009
OH, SEE, I KNOW
WHAT YOU NEED.

99
00:04:19,051 --> 00:04:20,301
YOU NEED A BODYGUARD.

100
00:04:20,343 --> 00:04:23,430
ROSS, WHAT IS BEN DOING
AFTER PRESCHOOL?

101
00:04:23,471 --> 00:04:25,766
OKAY, LISTEN--
JOEY IS HAVING A PROBLEM...

102
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:28,977
WITH A LITTLE GIRL
WHO'S BEATING HIM UP.

103
00:04:29,019 --> 00:04:31,105
AW... JOEY, COME HERE.

104
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:32,981
LOOK-- HONEY, I KNOW
THIS MUST BE

105
00:04:33,023 --> 00:04:35,025
REALLY, REALLY DIFFICULT
FOR YOU...

106
00:04:35,067 --> 00:04:37,527
OH, I'M SORRY.
AM I HURTING YOU?

107
00:04:40,614 --> 00:04:42,241
( blowing )

108
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,951
( knocking )

109
00:04:46,578 --> 00:04:47,829
HEY!

110
00:04:47,871 --> 00:04:50,331
HEY! I BROUGHT YOU
SOME HOUSEWARMING GIFTS.

111
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:51,708
OH...

112
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:53,752
YEAH-- SALT, SO YOUR LIFE
ALWAYS HAS FLAVOR...

113
00:04:53,794 --> 00:04:54,836
OH.

114
00:04:54,878 --> 00:04:56,504
BREAD, SO YOU NEVER
GO HUNGRY...

115
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:57,672
OH...

116
00:04:57,714 --> 00:05:00,508
AND A SCENTED CANDLE
FOR THE BATHROOM

117
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:02,343
BECAUSE, WELL, YOU KNOW.

118
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:06,723
WELL, THANKS, THANKS,
AND... THANKS, I GUESS.

119
00:05:06,765 --> 00:05:08,349
YEAH!

120
00:05:08,391 --> 00:05:09,434
HI.
HI.

121
00:05:09,476 --> 00:05:10,936
WELCOME TO THE BUILDING.

122
00:05:10,978 --> 00:05:13,521
I'M STEVE SERRA, PRESIDENT
OF THE TENANTS COMMITTEE.

123
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:14,606
OH, HI. ROSS GELLER.

124
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:16,191
AND THIS IS MY FRIEND,
PHOEBE.

125
00:05:16,233 --> 00:05:17,317
HI, PHOEBE.

126
00:05:17,358 --> 00:05:19,402
MR. PRESIDENT.

127
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:22,864
I, UH, CAME TO TALK
TO YOU ABOUT HOWARD.

128
00:05:22,906 --> 00:05:24,158
HOWARD?

129
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:25,659
YEAH. HE'S THE HANDYMAN.

130
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,953
HE'S RETIRING NEXT WEEK,
AND EVERYONE WHO LIVES HERE

131
00:05:27,995 --> 00:05:29,621
IS KICKING IN
A HUNDRED BUCKS

132
00:05:29,663 --> 00:05:32,040
AS A "THANK YOU FOR
ALL OF THE HARD WORK"
TYPE OF THING.

133
00:05:32,082 --> 00:05:33,541
OH, THAT'S NICE.

134
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:35,294
YEAH. YOU WANT TO GIVE
ME A CHECK OR...?

135
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:37,712
( chuckling ):
OH! UH...

136
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,338
LOOK, YOU DON'T

137
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,715
HAVE TO GIVE IT
TO ME RIGHT NOW.

138
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:42,092
YOU CAN SLIP IT
UNDER MY DOOR...

139
00:05:42,134 --> 00:05:43,844
NO, NO, IT'S NOT THAT.

140
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:46,930
IT'S JUST, I...
I-I JUST MOVED IN.

141
00:05:46,972 --> 00:05:51,059
WELL, THE GUY'S WORKED
HERE FOR 25 YEARS.

142
00:05:51,101 --> 00:05:53,854
YES, BUT I'VE LIVED HERE
FOR 25 MINUTES.

143
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:55,772
OH.

144
00:05:55,814 --> 00:05:57,191
( Ross chuckles )

145
00:05:57,232 --> 00:05:59,776
OKAY. I GET IT.

146
00:05:59,818 --> 00:06:01,402
NO, WAIT. LOOK, LOOK...

147
00:06:01,444 --> 00:06:04,823
I'M SORRY, IT'S JUST I'VE
NEVER EVEN MET... HOWARD.

148
00:06:04,865 --> 00:06:07,408
I MEAN, I DON'T KNOW HOWARD.

149
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:10,578
HOWARD'S THE HANDYMAN?

150
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:13,957
YES, BUT TO ME HE'S JUST...

151
00:06:13,999 --> 00:06:15,250
MAN.

152
00:06:15,292 --> 00:06:17,169
OKAY, FINE.

153
00:06:17,211 --> 00:06:19,171
WHATEVER.

154
00:06:19,213 --> 00:06:22,049
( coldly ):
WELCOME TO THE BUILDING.

155
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:23,258
( scoffing )

156
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,426
CAN YOU BELIEVE THAT GUY?

157
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:29,348
YEAH. I REALLY LIKE
HIS GLASSES.

158
00:06:34,144 --> 00:06:36,437
...SO THEN PRESIDENT
STEVE TOLD EVERYONE

159
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:37,647
I WAS A CHEAPSKATE

160
00:06:37,689 --> 00:06:39,733
AND NOW THE WHOLE
BUILDING HATES ME.

161
00:06:39,774 --> 00:06:42,610
YOU KNOW, A LITTLE KID
SPIT ON MY KNEE.

162
00:06:42,652 --> 00:06:44,779
YOU KNOW WHAT
I'M GOING TO DO?

163
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:46,573
I'M GOING TO THROW
A PARTY--

164
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:48,950
THAT'S RIGHT,
FOR EVERYONE
IN THE BUILDING.

165
00:06:48,992 --> 00:06:50,618
I'M GOING TO SIT
THEM ALL DOWN

166
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:53,038
AND EXPLAIN TO THEM THAT
I AM NOT A BAD GUY.

167
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,248
I AM NOT A CHEAP GUY.

168
00:06:54,289 --> 00:06:56,583
I'M JUST A GUY
WHO-WHO STANDS UP

169
00:06:56,624 --> 00:06:58,210
FOR WHAT HE BELIEVES
IN, A MAN...

170
00:06:58,252 --> 00:07:00,170
( tapping finger ):
WITH PRINCIPLES.

171
00:07:00,212 --> 00:07:02,881
SOUNDS LIKE A FUN PARTY.

172
00:07:02,923 --> 00:07:05,508
LOOK, ROSS, IF YOU WANT
YOUR NEIGHBORS TO LIKE YOU

173
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:07,886
WHY DON'T YOU JUST PAY
THE HUNDRED BUCKS?

174
00:07:07,928 --> 00:07:10,638
A PARTY'S GOING TO COST YOU
WAY MORE THAN THAT.

175
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,349
THAT DOESN'T MATTER.

176
00:07:12,391 --> 00:07:14,017
IT'S MY PRINCIPLES.

177
00:07:14,059 --> 00:07:16,144
WE'RE TALKING
ABOUT MY PRINCIPLES!

178
00:07:16,186 --> 00:07:17,645
OKAY.

179
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:19,814
I THOUGHT IT WAS ABOUT
YOUR NEIGHBORS LIKING YOU.

180
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:23,860
OH, THEY'LL LIKE ME ONCE THEY
COME TO MY AWESOME PAR-TAY.

181
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:25,612
OKAY, I GOT TO RUN.

182
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:27,488
I GOT TO GO GET SOME NAME TAGS.

183
00:07:29,283 --> 00:07:30,992
( door closes )

184
00:07:31,034 --> 00:07:34,955
AND THAT CRAZY PARTY ANIMAL
WILL BE YOUR BROTHER-IN-LAW.

185
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:36,497
OH, YEAH. VERY, VERY FUNNY.

186
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:39,000
BUT DON'T SAY THINGS LIKE THAT
IN FRONT OF MONICA.

187
00:07:39,042 --> 00:07:41,460
I DON'T WANT YOU PUTTING
ANY IDEAS IN HER HEAD.

188
00:07:41,502 --> 00:07:43,422
UM, CHANDLER,
YOU-YOU DO REALIZE

189
00:07:43,462 --> 00:07:46,425
THAT THOSE IDEAS ARE PROBABLY
ALREADY IN MONICA'S HEAD?

190
00:07:46,465 --> 00:07:49,386
WH-WHY?

191
00:07:49,428 --> 00:07:53,765
WELL, BECAUSE SHE LOVES YOU
AND BECAUSE YOU LOVE HER.

192
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:56,351
YEAH? SO? WHAT'S THAT'S
SUPPOSED TO MEAN?

193
00:07:56,393 --> 00:07:58,145
HEY, CHANDLER, DON'T FREAK OUT.

194
00:07:58,186 --> 00:08:00,647
I'M TELLING YOU SOMETHING
YOU ALREADY KNOW.

195
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:02,565
COME ON, SHE BROKE UP
WITH RICHARD

196
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:04,692
BECAUSE HE DIDN'T WANT
TO HAVE BABIES

197
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:07,946
AND SHE'S A WOMAN, AND SHE'S
ALMOST 30, AND, YOU KNOW...

198
00:08:07,988 --> 00:08:09,656
IT'S MONICA.

199
00:08:09,697 --> 00:08:12,159
I DON'T SEE IT THAT WAY, OKAY?
BECAUSE I SEE TWO MONICAS--

200
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:14,535
THE ONE THAT WAS MY FRIEND
WHO LIVES ACROSS THE HALL

201
00:08:14,577 --> 00:08:16,330
AND WANTED TO HAVE
A LOT OF BABIES...

202
00:08:16,371 --> 00:08:19,458
AND THEN THE NEW MONICA,
WHO I JUST STARTED TO DATE.

203
00:08:19,498 --> 00:08:23,628
OKAY, NOW, WHO'S TO SAY
WHAT SHE WANTS?

204
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:25,172
I'M RIGHT. I'M RIGHT.

205
00:08:25,213 --> 00:08:27,382
AM I RIGHT?

206
00:08:29,134 --> 00:08:31,510
YEAH, YOU'RE RIGHT,
YOU ARE ABSOLUTELY RIGHT.

207
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:33,638
I MEAN, THAT MAKES
EVERYTHING DIFFERENT.

208
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:34,639
OKAY.

209
00:08:34,681 --> 00:08:35,807
( opens pop top )

210
00:08:35,849 --> 00:08:37,351
IT'S NOT DIFFERENT
AT ALL, IS IT?

211
00:08:37,392 --> 00:08:39,811
NOT UNLESS "DIFFERENT" MEANS
"THE SAME."

212
00:08:40,979 --> 00:08:43,357
YOU WERE SO FUNNY
WITH THAT WAITER.

213
00:08:43,398 --> 00:08:45,359
YOU'RE SUCH A NUT!

214
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:52,949
WELL, YOU KNOW,
BREADSTICK FANGS

215
00:08:52,991 --> 00:08:54,368
ARE ALWAYS FUNNY, SO...

216
00:08:54,409 --> 00:08:56,077
NO, YOU MAKE THEM FUNNY.

217
00:08:56,119 --> 00:08:58,121
YOU'RE THE FUNNY ONE!

218
00:08:58,163 --> 00:08:59,747
THANKS.

219
00:08:59,789 --> 00:09:02,250
UH, LOOK, KATIE, UH...

220
00:09:02,292 --> 00:09:04,336
LISTEN, WE-WE NEED
TO TALK, OKAY?

221
00:09:04,378 --> 00:09:07,047
UM, LOOK, I LIKE YOU--
I-I REALLY DO.

222
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:09,466
I LIKE YOU A LOT, OKAY?

223
00:09:09,508 --> 00:09:12,802
BUT SOMETIMES WHEN YOU
PLAYFULLY PUNCH ME LIKE THAT

224
00:09:12,844 --> 00:09:15,305
IT-IT FEELS LIKE
SOMEONE'S HITTING ME

225
00:09:15,347 --> 00:09:18,517
WITH A VERY TINY,
BUT A VERY REAL BAT.

226
00:09:18,558 --> 00:09:21,769
OH... LIKE I COULD HURT YOU.

227
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:24,147
ARE YOU MAKING FUN
OF MY SIZE?

228
00:09:24,189 --> 00:09:25,399
NO.

229
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:29,361
DON'T MAKE FUN OF ME
BECAUSE OF MY SIZE!

230
00:09:29,403 --> 00:09:31,821
YEAH, OKAY.

231
00:09:31,863 --> 00:09:32,864
OH...

232
00:09:32,906 --> 00:09:34,615
HMM...

233
00:09:34,657 --> 00:09:35,950
ISN'T THIS GREAT?

234
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:37,202
MMM.

235
00:09:37,244 --> 00:09:40,205
COULDN'T YOU JUST STAY
LIKE THIS FOREVER?

236
00:09:42,416 --> 00:09:44,000
CHANDLER?

237
00:09:44,042 --> 00:09:46,669
COULDN'T YOU JUST
STAY HERE FOREVER?

238
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:50,173
YEAH, HERE, SOMEWHERE ELSE...
YOU KNOW, WHERE-WHEREVER.

239
00:09:50,215 --> 00:09:51,508
( nervous chuckle )

240
00:09:51,550 --> 00:09:53,134
ARE YOU OKAY?

241
00:09:53,176 --> 00:09:54,511
YEAH. I'M COOL.

242
00:09:54,553 --> 00:09:56,346
CASUAL.

243
00:09:56,388 --> 00:09:58,681
WHAT-WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

244
00:09:58,723 --> 00:10:00,892
OH, JUST HANGING OUT,
YOU KNOW, HAVING FUN...

245
00:10:00,934 --> 00:10:03,395
YOU KNOW, WITH THE GIRL
THAT I'M SEEING CASUALLY.

246
00:10:03,437 --> 00:10:05,646
( scoffing ):
OH... MAN, I KNEW IT.

247
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:07,732
I KNEW YOU WERE GOING
TO DO THIS.

248
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:09,317
WHAT?
GET ALL FREAKED OUT

249
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:11,361
BECAUSE EVERYBODY WAS TALKING
AND JUST JOKING AROUND

250
00:10:11,403 --> 00:10:12,695
ABOUT MARRIAGE AND STUFF.

251
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:16,324
WELL, YOU-YOU DO WANT
ALL THAT STUFF, RIGHT?

252
00:10:16,366 --> 00:10:17,992
OH, AND YOU KNOW WHAT I WANT.

253
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:19,578
YES. YOU WANT BABIES.

254
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:21,162
YOU HAVE BABY FEVER.

255
00:10:21,204 --> 00:10:24,374
I DO NOT HAVE BABY FEVER.

256
00:10:24,416 --> 00:10:27,210
OH, PLEASE. YOU ARE OBSESSED
WITH BABIES AND MARRIAGE

257
00:10:27,252 --> 00:10:29,546
AND EVERYTHING THAT'S
RELATED TO BABIES

258
00:10:29,588 --> 00:10:30,880
AND-AND... MARRIAGE.

259
00:10:30,922 --> 00:10:33,091
YOU KNOW WHAT?
I GOT A GOOD IDEA.

260
00:10:33,133 --> 00:10:35,218
WHY DON'T WE TURN
THE HEAT DOWN

261
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:37,220
ON THIS
PRESSURE COOKER?!

262
00:10:37,262 --> 00:10:38,721
HAVE YOU LOST YOUR MIND?

263
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:41,266
CHANDLER, THIS ISN'T ABOUT ME;
THIS IS ABOUT YOU

264
00:10:41,308 --> 00:10:43,851
AND ALL YOUR WEIRD
RELATIONSHIP COMMITMENT CRAP.

265
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:45,228
NUH-UH. I KNOW YOU, OKAY?

266
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:46,605
I KNOW THE THOUGHTS

267
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:48,565
THAT YOU HAVE
IN THE HEAD--
IN YOUR HEAD.

268
00:10:48,607 --> 00:10:50,233
WELL, YOU DON'T KNOW EVERYTHING.

269
00:10:50,275 --> 00:10:53,320
DID YOU KNOW THAT I'M GOING OUT
WITH RACHEL TONIGHT

270
00:10:53,361 --> 00:10:54,946
INSTEAD OF YOU, HMM?

271
00:10:54,988 --> 00:10:56,906
AND DID YOU KNOW THAT THE ONLY
BABY AROUND HERE IS YOU?

272
00:10:56,948 --> 00:10:57,991
AND DID YOU KNOW

273
00:10:58,032 --> 00:10:59,659
THAT I CAN'T EVEN
LOOK AT YOU RIGHT NOW?

274
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:03,955
YEAH, WELL, I DID NOT KNOW THAT.

275
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:10,337
THIS IS GOING
TO BE OKAY, RIGHT?

276
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:12,255
I MEAN, SHE'S NOT
GOING TO LEAVE ME.

277
00:11:12,297 --> 00:11:13,381
THIS IS FIXABLE.

278
00:11:13,423 --> 00:11:14,882
SURE.
ABSOLUTELY.

279
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:15,716
BY ME.

280
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:16,801
OH, NO.

281
00:11:16,843 --> 00:11:18,637
NO, NO, NO.

282
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:22,432
WELL, UNLESS YOU MAKE
SOME KIND OF BIG GESTURE.

283
00:11:22,474 --> 00:11:23,642
Joey:
YEAH, BIG, THOUGH.

284
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:26,436
UH-OH! SHH! THE MISSUS.

285
00:11:26,478 --> 00:11:29,856
GUNTHER, CAN I
GET A COFFEE?

286
00:11:31,608 --> 00:11:32,817
TO GO?

287
00:11:32,859 --> 00:11:34,194
LOOK, MONICA...

288
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:36,613
I'M STILL NOT DONE
NOT WANTING TO TALK TO YOU.

289
00:11:36,655 --> 00:11:37,989
JUST TELL ME
WHAT I NEED TO DO

290
00:11:38,031 --> 00:11:39,115
TO MAKE THINGS RIGHT.

291
00:11:39,157 --> 00:11:40,116
WHAT?

292
00:11:40,158 --> 00:11:41,493
THAT'S WHAT WE DO.

293
00:11:41,535 --> 00:11:44,371
I MESS UP, AND THEN YOU
TELL ME HOW TO FIX IT

294
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:48,291
AND THEN I DO, AND THEN YOU
THINK I'M ALL CUTE AGAIN.

295
00:11:48,333 --> 00:11:51,336
I'M REALLY TIRED OF BEING
YOUR RELATIONSHIP TUTOR.

296
00:11:51,378 --> 00:11:53,963
YOU'RE GOING TO HAVE
TO FIGURE THIS ONE OUT

297
00:11:54,005 --> 00:11:56,132
FOR YOURSELF, ALL RIGHT?

298
00:11:56,174 --> 00:11:57,925
IF YOU'RE TOO AFRAID
TO BE IN A REAL RELATIONSHIP

299
00:11:57,967 --> 00:11:59,302
THEN DON'T
BE IN ONE.

300
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:41,928
( chanting ):
HOWARD! HOWARD!
HOWARD! HOWARD!

301
00:12:41,969 --> 00:12:45,265
HOWARD! HOWARD!
HOWARD! HOWARD!

302
00:12:45,306 --> 00:12:47,016
HOWARD! HOWARD!

303
00:12:47,058 --> 00:12:50,019
HOWARD! HOWARD!
HOWARD! HOWARD!

304
00:12:50,061 --> 00:12:51,187
PHOEBE?

305
00:12:51,229 --> 00:12:52,188
HOWARD!
PHOEBE?

306
00:12:52,230 --> 00:12:54,982
HOWARD! YAY!
OH, HI, ROSS!

307
00:12:55,024 --> 00:12:57,694
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

308
00:12:57,736 --> 00:12:59,613
OH, I THOUGHT
THIS WAS YOUR PARTY

309
00:12:59,654 --> 00:13:02,031
AND IT TURNS OUT,
IT'S A PARTY FOR HOWARD.

310
00:13:02,073 --> 00:13:03,824
HE'S THE SWEETEST LITTLE MAN.

311
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:05,034
SEE YA, PHOEBE.

312
00:13:05,076 --> 00:13:07,912
OH, AND, HEY, THANKS
FOR CHIPPING IN.

313
00:13:07,954 --> 00:13:08,996
OH, SURE.

314
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:11,958
YOU CHIPPED IN?

315
00:13:11,999 --> 00:13:13,710
YEAH, UH-HUH. $100.

316
00:13:13,752 --> 00:13:16,379
PHOEBE, I-I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU GAVE HIM MONEY.

317
00:13:16,421 --> 00:13:19,257
I THOUGHT YOU AGREED
IT WAS TRULY UNREASONABLE

318
00:13:19,299 --> 00:13:21,301
THAT THEY ASKED ME
FOR THAT MONEY.

319
00:13:21,342 --> 00:13:23,344
YEAH, BUT THEY
DIDN'T ASK ME, YOU KNOW

320
00:13:23,386 --> 00:13:26,139
AND THIS WAY I'M JUST
THE EXOTIC, GENEROUS STRANGER

321
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,682
AND THAT'S ALWAYS FUN TO BE.

322
00:13:27,724 --> 00:13:30,518
YEAH, BUT YOU'RE
MAKING ME LOOK BAD.

323
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:31,770
NO, I'M NOT. NO.

324
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:33,521
IF ANYTHING, I'M MAKING
YOU LOOK BETTER.

325
00:13:33,563 --> 00:13:35,982
THEY'LL SEE YOU TALKING
TO ME, AND THAT'S, YOU KNOW.

326
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:38,067
I'M A HIT.

327
00:13:38,109 --> 00:13:39,068
HEY, PHEEBS.

328
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:40,111
HEY.

329
00:13:40,153 --> 00:13:41,988
OH, HEY, ROSS.

330
00:13:42,029 --> 00:13:43,239
UM, SAY, I WAS THINKING

331
00:13:43,281 --> 00:13:45,283
MAYBE YOU TWO COULD
SWITCH APARTMENTS

332
00:13:45,325 --> 00:13:47,494
'CAUSE PHOEBE'S MORE
OUR KIND OF PEOPLE.

333
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:48,911
SOMETHING TO THINK ABOUT.

334
00:13:52,499 --> 00:13:54,709
YEAH, OKAY, MY BAD.

335
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,303
HEY.

336
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:06,387
HI.

337
00:14:09,432 --> 00:14:13,060
WOW, YOU LOOK...
YOU LOOK BIG.

338
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:15,396
THANKS. I'VE BEEN WORKING OUT.

339
00:14:15,438 --> 00:14:19,609
HEY, LISTEN, IS IT OBVIOUS
I'M WEARING SIX SWEATERS?

340
00:14:19,651 --> 00:14:24,071
UH, YEAH. BUT IT'S
NOT OBVIOUS WHY.

341
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:26,282
WELL, LOOK, I'M BREAKING UP
WITH KATIE.

342
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:28,451
SO I HAD TO PUT ON
SOME EXTRA PADDING.

343
00:14:28,493 --> 00:14:30,537
I MEAN, IF SHE HITS ME
WHEN SHE'S HAPPY

344
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:33,122
CAN YOU IMAGINE HOW HARD
SHE'S GOING TO HIT ME

345
00:14:33,164 --> 00:14:36,042
WHEN I TELL HER
I'M TAKING AWAY THE JOEY LOVE?

346
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:38,837
HEY.
HEY.

347
00:14:38,877 --> 00:14:39,838
HOW ARE YOU?

348
00:14:39,878 --> 00:14:42,382
HEY, CUTE JACKET.

349
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:44,175
OH, THANKS.

350
00:14:44,217 --> 00:14:45,552
THAT'S SO SWEET.
WHOA.

351
00:14:45,593 --> 00:14:46,553
OW!

352
00:14:46,594 --> 00:14:48,095
( laughing )

353
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:51,599
OH, "OW." DID JOEY
TELL YOU TO SAY THAT?

354
00:14:51,641 --> 00:14:53,560
YOU GUYS
ARE TOO MUCH.

355
00:14:53,601 --> 00:14:54,935
WHOA.

356
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:56,646
YOU KNOW WHAT, KATIE?

357
00:14:56,688 --> 00:14:58,565
I GOT TO TELL YOU.

358
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:03,069
I-I-I THINK YOU'RE
THE ONE THAT IS TOO MUCH.

359
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:05,321
OH, JOEY HAS
THE NICEST FRIENDS.

360
00:15:05,363 --> 00:15:09,992
OH, AND THE NICEST GIRLFRIEND.

361
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,745
OH...

362
00:15:11,786 --> 00:15:12,871
YOU'RE SO SWEET.

363
00:15:12,911 --> 00:15:15,415
WELL, YOU'RE SO SWEET.

364
00:15:15,456 --> 00:15:17,792
OW!

365
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:25,425
JOEY... SHE
JUST KICKED ME.

366
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:28,094
HUH.

367
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:31,556
WELL?

368
00:15:31,598 --> 00:15:33,266
AREN'T YOU GOING
TO DO SOMETHING?

369
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:34,267
UH...

370
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:35,685
YOU'D BETTER DO SOMETHING

371
00:15:35,727 --> 00:15:37,604
OR I'M GOING TO WALK
OUT THAT DOOR RIGHT NOW.

372
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,397
WELL?

373
00:15:39,439 --> 00:15:40,732
ARE YOU GONNA?

374
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:44,360
NAH.

375
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:57,540
( laughing )

376
00:15:57,582 --> 00:15:58,625
PHOEBE?

377
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:00,752
THAT'S WHAT
I WAS SAYING.

378
00:16:00,794 --> 00:16:02,086
PHOEBE, PHOEBE...

379
00:16:02,128 --> 00:16:03,254
OOH.

380
00:16:03,296 --> 00:16:04,881
LOOK, THIS IS A DISASTER.

381
00:16:04,923 --> 00:16:06,925
CAN'T I PLEASE
JUST GO?

382
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:08,635
NO, NO. I'M TALKING
YOU UP TO PEOPLE.

383
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:10,470
JUST GIVE IT
A LITTLE TIME, ALL RIGHT?

384
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:11,805
RELAX. GET SOMETHING TO EAT.

385
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:13,013
OKAY?

386
00:16:14,849 --> 00:16:16,225
SO, UH, WHAT

387
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:18,352
DID YOU TELL
THEM ABOUT ME?

388
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:20,730
UM, OH, I WAS TELLING THEM
ABOUT YOU AND EMILY.

389
00:16:20,772 --> 00:16:22,482
YOU KNOW, TRY
TO GET SOME SYMPATHY?

390
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:24,484
BUT SOMEHOW YOU CAME OFF
AS THE BAD GUY.

391
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:26,444
WHAT?

392
00:16:26,486 --> 00:16:27,821
YEAH. I THINK
I TOLD IT WRONG.

393
00:16:29,113 --> 00:16:30,865
YOU KNOW, WE SHOULD TALK
ABOUT THAT

394
00:16:30,907 --> 00:16:32,742
'CAUSE I DON'T TOTALLY
UNDERSTAND

395
00:16:32,784 --> 00:16:34,034
WHAT HAPPENED THERE.

396
00:16:35,453 --> 00:16:37,789
OOH, THIS CAKE
IS REALLY GOOD.

397
00:16:37,831 --> 00:16:40,249
SEE? THINGS
ARE LOOKING UP ALREADY.

398
00:16:40,291 --> 00:16:43,837
OH, MY GOD, SOMEONE
CUT HOWARD'S CAKE.

399
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:51,051
WHO WOULD DO
A THING LIKE THAT?

400
00:16:55,974 --> 00:16:57,851
3-B.

401
00:16:57,892 --> 00:16:59,477
All:
OH, YEAH. AW, COME ON.

402
00:16:59,519 --> 00:17:03,105
OKAY, YOU GOT YOUR FREE FOOD,
YOU RUINED EVERYONE'S FUN.

403
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:05,065
DON'T YOU THINK IT'S TIME
YOU WENT HOME?

404
00:17:05,107 --> 00:17:06,693
All:
HEY, GO HOME.

405
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:09,320
GO BACK TO 3-B, 3-B.

406
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:10,780
OKAY, EVERYONE?

407
00:17:10,822 --> 00:17:12,239
EVERYONE CALM DOWN.

408
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:14,868
I HAVE SOMETHING
THAT I WOULD LIKE TO SAY.

409
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:19,288
WHO HERE LIKES ROSS?

410
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:26,462
WELL, OF COURSE
YOU DON'T LIKE HIM.

411
00:17:26,504 --> 00:17:28,339
HE DIDN'T GIVE YOU ANY MONEY.

412
00:17:28,381 --> 00:17:32,010
HE RAISED HIS OWN HAND WHEN I
ASKED, "WHO HERE LIKES ROSS?"

413
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:34,094
AND HE'S WEARING TWO NAME TAGS.

414
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:38,725
I'LL BE HONEST WITH YOU GUYS.

415
00:17:38,766 --> 00:17:41,352
WHEN I FIRST MET ROSS,
I DIDN'T LIKE HIM AT ALL.

416
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:45,439
BUT THEN,
ONCE I GOT TO KNOW HIM

417
00:17:45,481 --> 00:17:48,108
I SAW THAT HE'S REALLY SWEET
AND CARING

418
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:50,570
AND VERY GENEROUS.

419
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:52,739
I MEAN, ALL I'M SAYING
IS DON'T JUDGE ROSS

420
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,574
BEFORE YOU GET TO KNOW HIM,
ALL RIGHT?

421
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:57,076
I MEAN, YOU KNOW, I LIKE
ALL YOU GUYS NOW

422
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:59,746
BUT WHEN I FIRST MET YOU,
YOU KNOW... CURT--

423
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:00,830
I THOUGHT, YOU KNOW

424
00:18:00,872 --> 00:18:02,289
"ABRASIVE DRUNK."

425
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:05,668
UM, LOLA--

426
00:18:05,710 --> 00:18:08,087
"MIND-NUMBINGLY STUPID."

427
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:09,505
YOU KNOW, AND...

428
00:18:09,547 --> 00:18:10,757
OKAY, YOU GUYS

429
00:18:10,798 --> 00:18:14,134
"GOLD-DIGGER,"
"CRADLE-ROBBING PERV."

430
00:18:15,678 --> 00:18:19,015
SO I THINK YOU ALL KNOW
WHAT I MEAN.

431
00:18:24,896 --> 00:18:26,439
OBVIOUSLY, I
DIDN'T THINK

432
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:29,191
THEY WERE GOING TO START
THROWING THINGS.

433
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:30,693
I JUST THOUGHT

434
00:18:30,735 --> 00:18:32,070
IF I KEPT
INSULTING THEM

435
00:18:32,110 --> 00:18:34,154
YOU WOULD JUMP IN
AND DEFEND EVERYONE

436
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:36,449
AND THEN YOU COULD
LOOK LIKE THE HERO.

437
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:38,409
OH, WOW, YEAH.

438
00:18:38,451 --> 00:18:41,079
SEE, I DID NOT GET THAT.

439
00:18:44,999 --> 00:18:45,959
WHERE'S MONICA?

440
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,126
I NEED TO TALK TO HER.

441
00:18:47,167 --> 00:18:48,628
IT'S URGENT. IS SHE HERE?

442
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:50,671
I'M MONICA.

443
00:18:50,713 --> 00:18:52,590
I NEED TO TALK TO YOU.
IT'S URGENT.

444
00:18:52,632 --> 00:18:53,841
OKAY.

445
00:18:53,883 --> 00:18:55,718
OKAY, I'VE BEEN DOING
A LOT OF THINKING

446
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:59,430
ABOUT US, YOU KNOW,
A LOT OF, UH, "US" THINKING

447
00:18:59,472 --> 00:19:02,976
AND, UH... WELL, I GUESS
THERE'S ONLY ONE...

448
00:19:03,017 --> 00:19:04,644
ONE WAY TO DO THIS.

449
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:06,687
NO, NO, NO.

450
00:19:06,729 --> 00:19:09,983
WH-WHAT...? WHAT
ARE YOU DOING?

451
00:19:10,024 --> 00:19:11,067
MONICA...

452
00:19:11,109 --> 00:19:12,485
NO, NO, NO. DON'T...
DON'T DO IT.

453
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:14,278
WILL YOU MARRY ME?

454
00:19:17,448 --> 00:19:19,117
OH, NO, NO, NO, NO.

455
00:19:19,158 --> 00:19:20,576
WHAT A BAD IDEA.

456
00:19:20,618 --> 00:19:22,787
OH, I CAN'T
NOT LOOK AT IT.

457
00:19:22,829 --> 00:19:26,707
CHANDLER, WHY ARE
YOU DOING THIS?

458
00:19:26,749 --> 00:19:27,875
I DON'T KNOW.

459
00:19:27,917 --> 00:19:31,504
BUT I KNOW I'M NOT
AFRAID TO DO THIS.

460
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:32,964
CHANDLER...

461
00:19:33,006 --> 00:19:36,342
I'M DOING THIS
BECAUSE I'M SORRY?

462
00:19:36,383 --> 00:19:39,386
D-DO YOU, UM,
YOU REALLY THINK

463
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,305
THE BEST REASON
TO GET MARRIED

464
00:19:41,347 --> 00:19:42,890
IS BECAUSE YOU'RE SORRY?

465
00:19:42,932 --> 00:19:44,976
WELL, NO. THE BEST REASON
TO GET MARRIED

466
00:19:45,018 --> 00:19:46,435
IS PREGNANCY.

467
00:19:48,312 --> 00:19:50,439
BUT "SORRY"
IS PRETTY MUCH FOURTH

468
00:19:50,481 --> 00:19:52,399
YOU KNOW,
BEHIND "BEING READY"

469
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:54,861
AND "ACTUALLY WANTING
TO GET MARRIED."

470
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:56,236
WILL YOU BE MY WIFE?

471
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:59,824
CHANDLER, UM, I WANT YOU
TO TAKE JUST A MINUTE

472
00:19:59,866 --> 00:20:02,035
AND I WANT YOU
TO THINK ABOUT

473
00:20:02,076 --> 00:20:04,120
HOW RIDICULOUS
THIS SOUNDS.

474
00:20:07,707 --> 00:20:11,127
YEAH, I'M KIND OF WISHING
EVERYONE WASN'T HERE RIGHT NOW.

475
00:20:11,169 --> 00:20:12,712
OH, HONEY,
DO YOU KNOW

476
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:15,381
THAT NONE OF THAT
STUFF CAME FROM ME?

477
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:17,133
I MEAN, I NEVER
SAID THAT I WANTED

478
00:20:17,175 --> 00:20:19,177
TO HAVE BABIES AND
GET MARRIED RIGHT NOW.

479
00:20:19,217 --> 00:20:21,095
YEAH, I KNOW, BUT I WAS
REALLY CONFUSED

480
00:20:21,137 --> 00:20:22,638
AND THEN I TALKED
TO THESE GUYS

481
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:25,183
WHO, TWO-DIVORCES
AND JOEY?

482
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:26,684
HEY.

483
00:20:26,726 --> 00:20:29,603
SHE'S RIGHT, YOU KNOW.

484
00:20:29,645 --> 00:20:32,732
YEAH, BUT STILL,
CHEAP SHOT.

485
00:20:34,734 --> 00:20:36,069
YOU KNOW WHAT?

486
00:20:36,110 --> 00:20:38,362
YOU WHEN I WHEN I SAID
THAT I WANT YOU TO DEAL

487
00:20:38,404 --> 00:20:40,865
WITH THIS RELATIONSHIP
STUFF ALL ON YOUR OWN?

488
00:20:40,907 --> 00:20:42,700
WELL, YOU'RE NOT
READY FOR THAT.

489
00:20:42,742 --> 00:20:45,661
I DIDN'T THINK I WAS.

490
00:20:45,703 --> 00:20:46,787
COME HERE.

491
00:20:49,456 --> 00:20:50,791
OH, MY GOD.

492
00:20:50,833 --> 00:20:54,253
WHAT WOULD YOU HAVE DONE
IF I HAD SAID YES?

493
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:56,005
WELL, I WOULD HAVE BEEN HAPPY

494
00:20:56,047 --> 00:20:58,465
BECAUSE I WOULD HAVE BEEN ABLE
TO SPEND THE REST OF MY LIFE

495
00:20:58,507 --> 00:21:01,052
WITH THE WOMAN THAT I LOVE.

496
00:21:01,094 --> 00:21:03,554
OR YOU WOULD HAVE SEEN
A CHANDLER-SHAPED HOLE

497
00:21:03,596 --> 00:21:04,931
IN THAT DOOR.

498
00:21:11,311 --> 00:21:13,189
WOULD YOU PASS ME
THAT KNIFE?

499
00:21:13,231 --> 00:21:14,481
NO, I WILL NOT.

500
00:21:14,523 --> 00:21:17,026
YOU DON'T HAVE TO
BE MEAN ABOUT IT.

501
00:21:17,068 --> 00:21:18,736
YOU'RE RIGHT. I'M SORRY.

502
00:21:18,778 --> 00:21:20,320
WILL YOU MARRY ME?

503
00:21:23,323 --> 00:21:25,243
I WAS GOING TO ASK YOU
TO MARRY ME

504
00:21:25,283 --> 00:21:27,870
'CAUSE I FORGOT TO SAY HELLO
TO YOU LAST WEEK.

505
00:21:27,912 --> 00:21:29,580
OH, NO, WAIT,
PHEEBS, I THINK

506
00:21:29,622 --> 00:21:31,749
WITH SOMETHING LIKE THAT,
YOU JUST ASK THEM

507
00:21:31,791 --> 00:21:33,709
TO MOVE IN WITH YOU,
BUT I'M NOT SURE.

508
00:21:33,751 --> 00:21:34,919
CHANDLER?

509
00:21:34,961 --> 00:21:36,963
OKAY, HOW LONG
IS THIS GOING TO GO ON?

510
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:39,048
WELL, I THINK
THE LENGTH OF TEASING

511
00:21:39,090 --> 00:21:41,634
IS DIRECTLY RELATED
TO HOW INSANE YOU WERE

512
00:21:41,675 --> 00:21:43,552
SO A LONG TIME.

513
00:21:43,594 --> 00:21:45,179
THIS IS FUN.

514
00:21:45,221 --> 00:21:47,848
HEY, RACH, REMEMBER THAT WHOLE
"WE WERE ON A BREAK" THING?

515
00:21:47,890 --> 00:21:49,850
WELL, I'M SORRY.
WILL YOU MARRY ME?

516
00:21:49,892 --> 00:21:51,227
( only Ross laughs )

517
00:21:51,269 --> 00:21:52,812
( laughter trails off )

518
00:21:55,522 --> 00:21:57,650
All:
THAT'S NOT FUNNY.

519
00:21:57,691 --> 00:22:00,653
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

